  "content": "Floods block Maidhar–Dudhe section of Asian Highway in Jhapa\nOnlinekhabar\nSunday, October 5, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 5\nThe Maidhar–Dudhe road section in Jhapa, which is part of the under-construction East–West Asian Highway, has been blocked. Vehicular movement has been disrupted after floods in the Bhalukhola River swept away the diversion.\nVehicles using this route have been diverted. According to police, vehicles traveling from east to west are being rerouted from Maidhar through the southern Kanakai Canal to Sangam Chowk, while those traveling from west to east are being diverted from Sangam Chowk through the southern Kanakai Canal to Maidhara.\nRepair work on the damaged diversion has begun.\nSimilarly, floods in the Kali River have obstructed the highway section at Mechinagar Municipality–6, and floods in the Sukuna River have blocked the section at Shivasatakshi Municipality–10.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nCOVID-19 Nepal\nKP Sharma Oli\nNepal covid-19\nCPN-UML\nNepali Congress\nNepal\nNepalelection\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nIPPAN calls for high alert over flood threat\n3 months ago\n55 rescued, 18 missing after flood hits Rasuwagadhi\n3 months ago\nFlood alert issued as water level rises in Mohana River\n3 months ago\nIs the flood in Kavre just ‘normal’?\n5 months ago\nFlood hits Babarmahal after Melamchi water pipe bursts (Photo Feature)\n8 months ago\nBalkhu community reels from flood damage: ‘We thought we would die’\n1 year ago\nMost Read\nVarious ways you can enjoy goat meat this Dashain festival\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nNepalis celebrate Bijaya Dashami, auspicious Tika time set at 11:53 am\nManaslu climbing in autumn starts on encouraging note; Nima Chhiring sets new record\nMonsoon triggers flood and landslide risks in several districts, DHM issues special alert\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n2 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n2 months ago\nAlso Read\nDisaster\nNighttime vehicle movement banned indefinitely on Hetauda–Kathmandu short route\n11 hours ago\nDisaster\nHundreds stranded on Everest’s eastern side after heavy snowfall\n14 hours ago\nDisaster\nFloods and landslides obstruct roads at 19 locations in Koshi and Bagmati Provinces\n16 hours ago\nDisaster\nDeath toll from landslides and floods rises to 52 across Nepal\n1 day ago\nDisaster\nHeavy rain risk eases in Kathmandu Valley, shifts to Koshi Province\n2 days ago",
